/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148392 #edb/ref 1061 594276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148392 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2e343aa9-f699-5b3e-a382-effdfef6dd15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148392 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148393 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148393 #edb/ref 1061 594277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148393 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "29698ec0-1dda-5f69-bb67-f92175c1a371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148393 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148394 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148394 #edb/ref 1061 594280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148394 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7615658-7aa8-5de3-95ff-2d74b5889e16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148394 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148395 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148395 #edb/ref 1061 594283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148395 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "060c8c47-3b5f-5a36-b80e-757102d6f065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148395 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148396 #edb/ref 1061 594286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148396 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b0fcd37-0446-59cb-b89e-24c477e9a1cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148396 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148771 #edb/ref 1064 "There are three types of equilibrium solutions for an *autonomous* differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = f(y),\n$$\n\nwhere the right-hand side doesn't depend explicitly on $x.$\nWe can classify each using the differential equation's phase line.\n\nLet's see each type, and classify the equilibrium solutions for the differential equation whose phase line is shown below.\n\n![](images/c6/c6fc21e9c83b98e055751ebd4062a3019687a885e2561191ec2d0bfd9de36a85.png)\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a **sink** if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\nFor the phase line above, $y=2$ is a sink.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a **source** if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution. \nFor the phase line above, $y=0$ is a source.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a **node** if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\nFor the phase line above, $y=-2$ is a node since the arrows above and below it both point downward." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148771 #edb/ref 1065 5572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148771 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2f2f0bc9-a043-5c8e-92aa-88135e4033a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148771 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312195 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c7/c7e7fd7cbf8c3f2f9b68f0af3ecfbdb616730dc7b7cc3b03aa6f35228843080e.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312195 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312195 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d547b80-0952-51a1-876e-e4e3237a133b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312546 #edb/ref 1080 "images/51/514e6bec32ef0d172c5d3e9df05da8613806bb60faee267702ffa17238d0f826.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312546 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312546 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45f2ea4f-dc22-56e7-bc03-5ea01da64a0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313364 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c6/c697a6b80923ffb6c557d59aa2e2924561121c373b4221709e280e5d35297e33.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b2749a4e-2333-513b-a009-d0b54fb57f84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313851 #edb/ref 1080 "images/74/74032d1b543a7446e87b9d3c9b1737f61996cf32817a3bce4db26f229457a348.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313851 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313851 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eb719dc5-820f-5706-8579-b09db7a542d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313896 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ef/ef9ada6ab016d70b2b14d53cb2f3021793ea78dd69048700c07d5a5161901ecf.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313896 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313896 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "efe1924f-b6ff-5ccc-8cc3-150714e499b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314331 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7957c9fa-0c70-53b9-94b5-a3465912ab8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1071 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-2$ is a node\n\n- $y=1$ is a source\n\n- $y=3$ is a sink\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24eff55c-c123-528b-9b40-89bdd5a76ad5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314938 #edb/ref 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-2,$ $y=1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=1$ (already drawn by the above property) and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-2$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=-2$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just above $y=-2$ points downward, the arrow just below it points downward too.\n\n![](images/b2/b2cb0682ba91ac23d418d91e7564cbb6245bf498de79b3e615f3ed2b1fcdb997.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/74/74032d1b543a7446e87b9d3c9b1737f61996cf32817a3bce4db26f229457a348.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2,$ $y=1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking below the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking above the line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=1$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to converge toward this line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1080 "images/31/31519aa878fd6a9b450296552afd9bbf628e30db68a2d7c6dc6b02a48ae28b06.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "037a7d4f-c46b-5ef5-9f12-e499f543ede1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a3/a375a537b104f5bcdd8f5951277bce2494d8861a7212772a7d7050fa14091cb9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0562a68a-9113-579a-9191-136bc8b91243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360958 #edb/ref 1080 "$y=0$ is a source, and $y=2$ is a sink" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360958 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360958 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1dbe103d-5637-58d2-abc9-7a6c3e453573" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d7/d72110682c1959f10546b6fa49d6e4ebedf6b6d5557639c772f28a920f306df5.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361050 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f9fb8ad-c027-5308-86ad-a2260380cc77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361092 #edb/ref 1080 "$y=0$ and $y=2$ are both sources" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3827fd23-1329-5a2a-a0d6-8196083f2fa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361109 #edb/ref 1080 "images/41/41f32a097325dbe2a278da2abe4ef93b13d058ffe49431882fade3bc40bc0f48.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361109 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361109 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b5da285-1e73-5eac-bb63-ee605aca7f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361116 #edb/ref 1080 "$y=3$ is a sink" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361116 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361116 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3c7472dd-4374-53b0-ab00-c75e67df452a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361324 #edb/ref 1080 "$y=0$ is a source, and $y=2$ is a node" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1759218